1
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:17,200
Summer has come again this year.

2
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,860
It's here, it's here,
it's come, it's here, it's here.

3
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,140
Summer has come again this year.

4
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:25,340
It's here, it's come, it's here, it's come.

5
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:28,620
On the big road,
drinking it all up, yajuku-i no.

6
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,560
With a big chest,
pressed against the chest, yajuku-i no.

7
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:36,060
On the shore,

8
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,000
Summer has come again this year.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,580
It's here, it's come, it's here, it's here.

10
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:46,780
It's a bond like this.

11
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:48,700
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha-ha

12
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:52,360
big waves, small waves, tiny little waves,
about that size

13
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:55,280
good for the southern breeze too

14
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,420
big bottoms, small bottoms, tiny little ones,
about that size

15
00:00:58,420 --> 00:00:59,220
Axo

16
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:07,860
in the southern breeze

17
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:13,780
in the southern breeze

18
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:22,280
on the shore, on the shore, on the shore

19
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:31,960
Reiko, meteor of wrath!

20
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,260
Doki doki!

21
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:45,540
Yahoo!

22
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:52,340
The tachometer has hit the red
zone at one million rotations!

23
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:56,420
Now powering up to two million rotations!

24
00:01:57,560 --> 00:02:00,000
Sharp curve ahead, react quickly!

25
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:11,280
W-we're scared! Isn't this dangerous!

26
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:22,740
At corners, stop first.

27
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:25,120
checking that no cars are coming,

28
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:28,480
look right, look left,
and make sure it's safe.

29
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:29,260
Got it?

30
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:29,740
Run!

31
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,960
You can't just dash out.

32
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:37,160
Oh no.

33
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:37,780
Is that all right?

34
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,480
If you're late for your shift change,

35
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:45,900
Ryo-chan, you're being noisy.

36
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:46,660
Reiko-chan.

37
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,720
Hello, how's your uncle's cold?

38
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:51,860
His fever's gone down now,

39
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:54,520
so in two or three days
he'll be back at the shop.

40
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:56,460
It's been hard for Auntie on her own, too,

41
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,080
so take care of yourself.

42
00:02:58,580 --> 00:02:59,500
Well, get well soon.

43
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:00,020
Just a moment.

44
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:02,220
Thank you for always looking out for us.

45
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:04,400
We're really grateful to Reiko-chan,

46
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:06,660
so take this with you.
It's merchandise, but please have it.

47
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:11,600
I was told to be there at 12,
and now I'm totally late.

48
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:12,460
Yes.

49
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:13,620
Thank you very much.

50
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:17,240
What a good girl you are, Reiko-chan.

51
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:21,360
Good children who stop crying
right away are rare these days.

52
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:24,320
She's dependable,
and on top of that, she's a beauty.

53
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:27,300
I wish we could swap her for my daughter-in-law,
you know.

54
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:28,860
Really.

55
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:33,680
Wait a moment.

56
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,580
Come on, let's cross, Grandma.

57
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:39,170
Well,

58
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:43,280
there is a pedestrian bridge if you take the long way around,
you know.

59
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:47,280
It's a relief that there
are so many cars here, though.

60
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,780
A traffic light is going
to be installed here soon.

61
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:51,300
Please be patient a little longer.

62
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,960
Hurry up!

63
00:03:57,860 --> 00:03:59,280
Please wait just a moment.

64
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:00,820
Yes, yes.

65
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:06,520
What is it?

66
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:11,420
That grandma waited a long time to cross here,
you know.

67
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:13,500
If you'd just waited about thirty seconds,

68
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:15,100
Okay.

69
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,300
Thank you for your cooperation.

70
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:23,600
Thank you very much.

71
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,540
No, be careful.

72
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:31,460
Good. Reiko,
could you come here for a moment?

73
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,840
It's been like this
every day for a while now.

74
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:49,940
It's in front of a kindergarten, and children
get hidden behind the cars, so it's dangerous.

75
00:04:49,940 --> 00:04:52,240
I've warned them many times,
but they won't listen.

76
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,780
Isn't that in the middle of the crosswalk?

77
00:04:54,780 --> 00:04:55,740
How shameless!

78
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:59,660
That car with Adachi plates parked
in front of the kindergarten.

79
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:01,460
Please move it immediately.

80
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,460
So, that's the situation.

81
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,180
He's been running around.

82
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:24,400
He's at a repair shop nearby.

83
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,920
Shouldn't he be coming back soon?

84
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:27,440
These people.

85
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:29,340
He said the exact same thing yesterday, too.

86
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,640
Nothing but lies.

87
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:37,040
Give me a break, he's got no points left.

88
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:40,800
Aren't they adorable?
The parents of Kameari, I tell you.

89
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:44,780
Do they think they can get away without
showing a license or moving the car?

90
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:48,900
They're probably begging for mercy.

91
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:52,860
Then I'll move it for them.

92
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:03,040
What's that supposed to mean?

93
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:08,580
It's actually a cylinder
meant for jacking up cars, but

94
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:14,200
if you crank the level to the maximum,
it keeps inflating and inflating.

95
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:14,960
On!

96
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,120
Hey, hey, stop that!

97
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:35,940
I don't know how to stop it.
I've never used it before.

98
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,660
Damn it!

99
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:55,600
What?!

100
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:00,800
Haaah!

101
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:02,960
Yaaah!

102
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:06,180
Whoaaa!

103
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:08,280
Whoaaa!

104
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:10,780
Hey, put it down!

105
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:16,920
Such shapely legs!

106
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:25,700
Terrifying legs!

107
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,620
I'm not letting this go, you hear me?

108
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:33,900
Of course.

109
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:35,840
Make sure you pay the fine.

110
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:37,520
Uh-oh.

111
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:43,400
Welcome back.

112
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:45,920
You're late.

113
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:47,340
You're late.

114
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:49,320
Sorry, Ryo-chan.

115
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,960
Shift change is at noon.

116
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,660
It's already past one!

117
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:56,420
I'm completely worn out from
being on duty all this time.

118
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:58,520
Patrol is my life.

119
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:03,440
You say
"shift change," but you're here round the clock!

120
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:09,660
Since Chief Ohara isn't
coming to the station today,

121
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:11,480
he's been like this the whole time.

122
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:14,960
I'm heading out on patrol.

123
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:18,260
Speaking of which, I'm starving.

124
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,780
You haven't come back for ages.

125
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:26,600
I couldn't even go out for lunch, you know!

126
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:31,340
Hey, don't overcook the noodles.
Extra green onions, okay?

127
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:34,684
It's not like I forgot
about the shift change.

128
00:08:34,734 --> 00:08:36,320
It's been really hectic.

129
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:39,100
One thing after another.

130
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,280
Hey, Reiko.

131
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,380
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

132
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:45,460
Hand me that newspaper.

133
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:48,260
Wouldn't it be faster to grab it yourself?

134
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:50,979
There's this terrible violator,

135
00:08:51,029 --> 00:08:53,860
and no matter how many times I say it's an illegal parking violation,
he won't listen.

136
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:57,060
He's being disrespectful,
looking down on us right from the start.

137
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,820
While you're at it,
give my back a shiatsu massage.

138
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,480
Lower, it's lower!

139
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,960
Not there, there, right there!

140
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,140
Press firmly, push hard!

141
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:11,100
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

142
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:11,900
Like this?

143
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:16,040
No good, it's not working at all!

144
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:18,580
That's why people walk all over you.

145
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:20,820
That has nothing to do with it.

146
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:25,140
What patrol needs is the muscle
power that oozes from your face.

147
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:27,480
Your face has no muscle power at all.

148
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:30,600
It's itchy.

149
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:32,740
Scratch the spot just below there.

150
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:33,160
There?

151
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:34,820
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

152
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,440
Hey, is the ramen okay?

153
00:09:37,820 --> 00:09:39,240
Don't overcook it!

154
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,560
The itchy spot again...

155
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:43,680
What are you doing?

156
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:45,060
In the end, it's all about strength, right?

157
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:46,160
Here we go!

158
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:51,860
Ugh, how infuriating!
I'll get you back, just you wait!

159
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,160
I'll throw you off too, you'll see!

160
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:56,480
W-what is that?!

161
00:09:57,040 --> 00:10:00,200
A custom pillow for smacking Ryo-chan with,
handmade!

162
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:01,000
What?

163
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:02,820
How about it?

164
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,380
Never let your guard down!
Counterattack begins!

165
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:23,000
Feel the true strength of a man!

166
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,460
That's cruel!

167
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:27,700
Had enough?

168
00:10:30,560 --> 00:10:32,020
The match is just beginning!

169
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,260
If strength won't work,
I'll win with endurance!

170
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:42,460
Okay, okay! Enough! Don't kill me!

171
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,140
Not yet!

172
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:44,300
Again!

173
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,700
What a vindictive woman she is.

174
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:50,880
Yes.

175
00:10:53,700 --> 00:10:55,420
I saw the poster, but

176
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:57,640
Who are you trying to reach?

177
00:10:58,220 --> 00:10:59,800
You're looking for Reiko, right?

178
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,220
Who are you?

179
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:02,860
Please go on a date with me.

180
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:05,320
Who are you?

181
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,960
How did you get this number?

182
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:09,520
Well, it was written on the poster.

183
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:10,560
What's that supposed to mean?

184
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:11,580
What's wrong?

185
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:14,960
Yeah, some weird phone call
about a poster or something.

186
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:17,540
Hello?

187
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:18,640
Is this Reiko?

188
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:20,120
Who are you?

189
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:22,880
Want to go to the sea with me or something?

190
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:23,940
No, I don't.

191
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:25,500
Then, uh-oh.

192
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,060
Go alone.

193
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,007
What is this? It's making me furious.

194
00:11:30,057 --> 00:11:33,400
Asking for a date without even
introducing yourself is so rude.

195
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:34,480
A date?

196
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:36,560
All right, give it here.

197
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:38,980
Reiko?

198
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:41,060
Yeah, is it a date request?

199
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:42,280
Yes.

200
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:46,180
Right, first,
transfer 5,000 yen to me as a finder's fee.

201
00:11:46,660 --> 00:11:49,300
Keep talking nonsense and I'll arrest you.

202
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,080
Reiko.

203
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:53,680
There are loads of these posted outside.

204
00:11:54,540 --> 00:11:55,260
What's this?

205
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:13,880
So that's why those guys
called after seeing this.

206
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,860
A poorly done candid photo

207
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,580
Who would make something like this?

208
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:20,360
I've peeled off quite a few of them,

209
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:23,440
but they're still plastered all
over along the national highway.

210
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:25,400
Must be that bean guy.

211
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,600
Reiko, around here...

212
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:28,780
Of course there aren't any, obviously.

213
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:30,560
This is Naoko.

214
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:31,680
This is Naoko.

215
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:32,640
Come in.

216
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:33,700
Come in.

217
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:43,280
Spotted a suspicious large dump truck.

218
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:46,900
Currently tailing it,
heading north toward Kameari.

219
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,260
We need backup, please.

220
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:55,800
That driver was going around
plastering posters of Reiko everywhere.

221
00:12:57,320 --> 00:13:00,320
Roger! We'll pincer it and nail them down.

222
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,280
That's terrible.

223
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:16,160
It's Reiko's grand march!

224
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:29,800
The two of them are
properly checking the signal.

225
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:30,720
Good job, good job.

226
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:37,680
Reiko-san was pulled away by a stamp.

227
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:39,060
Can't you see it?

228
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:41,220
Aaaaaaah!

229
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:44,900
Do you think there is?

230
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:52,980
Tea together.

231
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:56,880
Aaaaaaah!

232
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:59,160
Aaaaaaah!

233
00:13:59,160 --> 00:13:59,480
Aaaaaaah!

234
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:27,920
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

235
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:28,700
I'm fine, I'm fine.

236
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:29,700
Thank goodness.

237
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:33,540
Mirror! I scraped my hand!

238
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:34,900
Ouch, ouch.

239
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:36,480
I hit my back too.

240
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:39,980
That's unforgivable!

241
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,040
Reiko, that's way too rough!

242
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:46,600
That hurts.

243
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:49,120
Hurry up and put your seatbelt on.

244
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,580
Reporting to you.

245
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:53,940
This is Ryotsu.

246
00:14:53,940 --> 00:14:56,780
Currently tailing a dump
truck with an Adachi plate.

247
00:14:57,920 --> 00:15:00,540
That driver was the one who put up Reiko's posters,
wasn't he?

248
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:00,882
Right,

249
00:15:00,932 --> 00:15:04,600
It's a pincer attack! You lot head
straight this way down Mito Kaido,

250
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:08,960
Use up your last shot,
and tell them to take care!

251
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,180
You're not getting away!

252
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:31,660
Found it!

253
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:34,140
Wide Jack! Hold position!

254
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,680
Aaaaah!

255
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:51,080
Aaaaah!

256
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,700
Aaaaah!

257
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,320
Aaaaah!

258
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:07,140
Just as the rumors said, what a disrespectful one!
What happened, Reiko? You two, we almost...

259
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:13,200
And what grudge do you
have against me, anyway?

260
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,700
N-no, I don't really have a grudge...

261
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:19,320
Then why did you go and
plaster posters all over town?

262
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:19,980
Reiko-san!

263
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:22,480
Look over there.

264
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,000
It's them!

265
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:26,880
Them?

266
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:28,820
Damn, they spotted us!

267
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:33,020
Since I knew you'd come,
I left the rest to you.

268
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:33,580
Yes!

269
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:34,740
Ryo-chan, hurry!

270
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:45,540
It's the car that was parked
in front of that kindergarten.

271
00:16:46,060 --> 00:16:47,840
Those are the vicious illegal parkers

272
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:50,660
Still, what a tacky car that is.

273
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:53,120
A natural monument like that, these days.

274
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:02,780
Broken down, my foot!

275
00:17:02,780 --> 00:17:04,540
It's running just fine, though!

276
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:05,100
Shut up!

277
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:09,240
Hey, don't let it get away!

278
00:17:10,340 --> 00:17:13,900
If it's come to this, we should have
done this more thoroughly back then!

279
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:20,380
Damn, that was a tough hit to take!

280
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:25,300
Your way of doing things is so wimpy,
isn't it?

281
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,500
You're the one being violent here!

282
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:30,060
Just because it's a used car,
don't get so cocky!

283
00:17:30,780 --> 00:17:33,400
If you have something to say, let's
go back to the station and hear it out!

284
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:34,260
That's right, that's right!

285
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:35,640
Don't back down!

286
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,340
Wait right there!

287
00:17:44,220 --> 00:17:45,380
Calm down, Reiko.

288
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:47,580
Look, I understand how you feel, but

289
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:50,500
A mini-patrol car is just a 550cc kei car.

290
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:53,060
There's no way we can catch up with those 2000cc guys,
you know.

291
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,920
Hey, they're still on our tail!

292
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:02,640
That's not just reckless driving, is it?

293
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,180
For a kei car to go that far is no joke.

294
00:18:05,180 --> 00:18:06,760
Let's just get on the expressway!

295
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:09,220
That car won't handle the expressway, so...

296
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,260
They've gotten away onto the expressway.

297
00:18:17,260 --> 00:18:18,840
We can't catch them in this car!

298
00:18:20,060 --> 00:18:20,760
This is Reiko.

299
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,760
Yes, this is Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo.

300
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,260
Kei-chan, I have a favor to ask.

301
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:32,180
I can't see them anymore.

302
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:33,700
Reiko.

303
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:38,700
Damn it.

304
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:40,080
Hurry up and stop them!

305
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:43,340
Eeeeeeh!

306
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:44,960
Eeeeeeh!

307
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:47,620
She's here, over here!

308
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:52,100
An Audi Quattro

309
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:54,340
Sorry I'm late.

310
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:57,120
It only arrived yesterday.

311
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:00,740
This is the car that won the Monte Carlo Rally,
you know.

312
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:04,300
I begged a collector to let me have it.

313
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:05,600
Well then, I'll borrow it.

314
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:18,060
It wasn't there a moment ago, but some weird
thing is chasing us instead of the mini-patrol car.

315
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:20,820
Hey, wait, could it be them?

316
00:19:25,980 --> 00:19:27,100
Ooh, we're coming to see you, dear.

317
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:28,940
Go, go, we're almost there.

318
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:29,760
Oh my.

319
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:31,220
What is it, what happened?

320
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:36,960
Looks like we're out of gas.
Ugh, how annoying.

321
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:41,760
What's wrong with Nakagawa? You should
keep the gas tank full at all times.

322
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:43,920
And there are no gas
stations on the expressway.

323
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:48,340
Found some gasoline!

324
00:19:48,820 --> 00:19:52,400
Reiko, slow down! We're taking it
from the tanker truck behind us!

325
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:02,980
What are those guys doing!

326
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:06,340
Damn it! The car ahead is too slow,
we can't get past!

327
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:10,500
At 100 yen a liter,
45 liters comes to 4,500 yen, right!

328
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:13,220
Reiko, make them pay 4,500 yen!

329
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:14,740
Bottoms are fine!

330
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:20,120
Fine? So you mean you don't want it?

331
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:23,280
Alright! I've got the change!

332
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:28,540
This is nothing!

333
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:33,360
Hurry up and hand over the money!
The change!

334
00:20:33,420 --> 00:20:33,860
Yoi-chan, hurry and take it!

335
00:20:36,780 --> 00:20:39,280
Give me the change! My money!

336
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:41,840
The change is mine!

337
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:46,440
Woah, my money!

338
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:51,540
Here they come again!

339
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:52,880
I can't take this anymore!

340
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:55,780
Damn it...

341
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:59,300
My money!

342
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:02,060
Damn it, brakes!

343
00:21:05,620 --> 00:21:07,700
Don't be naive! I won't let them get away!

344
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:09,960
Reiko, go! I allow it!

345
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:15,040
Wait a minute! Expressway!
Don't drive the wrong way!

346
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:17,420
You went too far, Reiko!

347
00:21:30,860 --> 00:21:31,960
Aaaaaaah!

348
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,540
Sakodan can't handle snow!

349
00:21:39,660 --> 00:21:42,160
How far can you climb in that car?

350
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:49,560
Stop it, Reiko!

351
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:53,720
Even with Audis, hooking two cars together
for a snowy slope is way too reckless!

352
00:22:11,980 --> 00:22:12,960
So scary!

353
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:17,880
Underestimate a woman
and you'll be in for it!

354
00:22:18,860 --> 00:22:21,840
You must never make an enemy of her.

355
00:22:23,740 --> 00:22:27,280
We got up here alright,
but I wonder what's happened to them?

356
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:29,633
Ah ah ah ah ah ah

357
00:22:29,683 --> 00:22:32,271
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

358
00:22:32,321 --> 00:22:34,885
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

359
00:22:34,935 --> 00:22:37,549
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

360
00:22:37,599 --> 00:22:40,151
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

361
00:22:40,201 --> 00:22:42,802
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

362
00:22:42,852 --> 00:22:45,429
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah,

363
00:22:45,479 --> 00:22:48,200
Ah ah ah ah ah ah ah, ah

364
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:48,740
Good work.

365
00:22:49,180 --> 00:22:50,720
What's gotten into those two?

366
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,640
They were totally won over
by Reiko's driving technique.

367
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:55,440
Apparently they became her
apprentices without asking.

368
00:22:56,700 --> 00:23:00,760
It's been ages since I was this terrified.

369
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:05,140
You all make sure to be
careful around Reiko, too.

370
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:06,080
Got it?

371
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:06,800
Yeah.

372
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:08,360
Did you call for Ryo-chan?

373
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:08,980
Don't slip up.

374
00:23:09,520 --> 00:23:10,960
Here's your tea.

375
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:14,200
Reiko-san,
thank you as always for the delicious tea.

376
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:15,560
Thank you.

377
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:16,120
Thank you.

378
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:18,840
Lovely weather.

379
00:23:20,180 --> 00:23:21,280
Be careful.

380
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:22,340
I know, I know.

381
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:26,600
It's the grandma from the other day!

382
00:23:26,600 --> 00:23:29,420
Thank you so much for
your kindness that time.

383
00:23:29,420 --> 00:23:30,660
You're welcome.

384
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:31,840
Reiko-chan.

385
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:34,280
Grandma, what's the matter?

386
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:37,460
Actually,
Reiko-chan has a good marriage proposal.

387
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:41,260
So you're a young lady of
marriageable age after all

388
00:23:41,260 --> 00:23:42,640
Grandma, you...

389
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:48,420
Hey, if she married someone like that,
she'd have a terrible time, wouldn't she?

390
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,480
This year is the Olympic year.

391
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:08,540
Speaking of the Olympics, there's Higurashi.

392
00:24:08,540 --> 00:24:12,060
Higurashi is a fellow officer
from the Kameari Park police box.

393
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:14,760
A lazy-bones patrolman, that's what he is.

394
00:24:14,760 --> 00:24:17,960
But he has an incredible psychic power.

395
00:24:18,460 --> 00:24:20,540
Next time: Awaken! The Hibernating Cop!

396
00:24:20,930 --> 00:24:21,440
Nice to meet you.

397
00:24:43,640 --> 00:24:45,400
Keep smiling, okay?

398
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:50,620
Just step out with a carefree face.

399
00:24:50,620 --> 00:24:54,120
Hey, give me a smile.

400
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:57,440
You're not wrong, you know.

401
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:02,860
Hey, give me a smile.

402
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:05,760
Keep up the same mood as before.

403
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:11,600
Keep smiling all the time, okay?

404
00:25:11,600 --> 00:25:16,560
Women who act all serious aren't pretty,

405
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:21,380
so you should smile right away.

406
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:25,860
Unless you're still a child.

407
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,800
Thank you for watching.

